# E-commerce Order Line
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: E-commerce — the individual Product/Quantity facts that make up an Order,
# same shape as accounting-journal-entry-line.menata
# Case 15 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# References: ecommerce-order.menata, ecommerce-product.menata
#
# Split out from ecommerce-order.menata (corrected 2026-07-11): originally an inline
# `Table of (...)` field on Order. Already fully expressible as an ordinary Object
# References pattern (001-object.md §Relationships) — "an Order has many Lines" is
# implied by "each Line references one Order," no separate grammar needed.

Order Line

Fields

- Order : Order
- Product : Product
- Quantity : Number
- Unit Price : Money
- Line Total : Money

Constraints

- Product is required.
- Quantity must be greater than zero.
- Line Total must equal Quantity times Unit Price.

Permissions

Customer

- View

Fulfillment

- View

Views

- Order Line List : List
- Order Line Detail : Detail
